<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $84.2 mln Feb 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $84.2 mln Feb 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $84.2 million deficit on Feb 20 in the commercial forex market, according to central bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 20</p>
<p>Exports: $151.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $214.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $285.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $307.1 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $84.2 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.198 million</p>
<p>Imports: $2.065 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.088 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.243 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $978 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
</text>
